 "title": "Carotenoid Synthesis and Gene Regulation in Rhodotorula Species",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on the carotenoid synthesis pathways and gene regulation in Rhodotorula species. R. glutinis ZHK and its orthologs R. diobovata, R. graminis, and R. taiwanensis share carotenoid synthesis pathways, producing β-carotene, torulene, torularhodin, and lycopene. The crtE, crtI, and crtYB genes are involved in carotenoid synthesis and are overexpressed in RtGGA. GGA uses NAT, pADH2, pGPD1, and other genes to regulate carotenoid synthesis. The cluster also includes enzymes involved in lipid production and resistance to G418 in IFO 0880.",
